---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="About me and my work.">
  <div class="about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I'm Dimitris Pantazis, a software developer from Greece. My non-Greek friends and coworkers call me <strong>Dimi</strong>.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Origin Story</h2>
      <p>
        I started writing code professionally in 2018, but my first encounter with it was back in 2008. I was 14, playing DOTA (Defense of the Ancients) in Warcraft 3.
      </p>
      <p>
        The community had built all sorts of bots, and I was one of those people for whom the bots weren't doing exactly what I wanted. So I had to dig into their code and figure out how they worked.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What I Do</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a Senior Software Engineer at <a href="https://stellarwp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">StellarWP</a>, where I help maintain and build new features for <a href="https://theeventscalendar.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Events Calendar</a> and other StellarWP products.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also take on projects through my agency <a href="https://pantadev.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Panta Dev</a>. If you're interested in working together, <a href="mailto:dimi@pantadev.com">reach out</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Expertise</h2>
      <p>
        I help businesses of all sizes with their software needs. It doesn't have to be WordPress — I work across a range of tools and frameworks.
      </p>
      <div class="tech-list">
        <span>Laravel</span>
        <span>Symfony</span>
        <span>React</span>
        <span>Next.js</span>
        <span>Vue</span>
        <span>Express</span>
        <span>NestJS</span>
        <span>WordPress</span>
        <span>WooCommerce</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        I've spent a lot of time in the WordPress ecosystem — as both a developer and a consultant — working with WooCommerce, The Events Calendar, Event Tickets, LearnDash, and more.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        I care about well-tested and documented code. Code should be easy to read, easy to maintain, and safe to update. No surprises.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
